embracing me, you will have occasion to see me afterwards, for I am not yet ascended to my Father, being to stay for some time upon earth; but go to my Brethren, and say unto them, I am alive, and in the way to ascend unto my Father and your Father, and to my God, and your God. Whereupon Mary Magdalene, and the other Women, having no room to doubt any longer, but, now that they had seen Jesus himself, being fully persuaded of the truth of the Resurrection, they immediately haste away to the Apostles and other Disciples, whom they found together all weeping and mourning in a hopeless manner, for those sad disappointments that had befallen them. And though they assured them from the testimony of three Angels, and that of their own Senses, that Jesus was risen, yet they believed them not, but continu'd to indulge their own melancholy prejudices, and look'd upon all the accounts which the Women gave them, as mere idle reports not to be regarded.
